{#
  A list cell that cannot wreck the table: the first item as a chip, plus a
  "+n" chip whose title carries the rest.

  The API-key tables used to print the raw JSON array the `scopes` column
  stores. That is one unbreakable ~120-character string with no spaces in it,
  so the cell's `max-width` did nothing, the table grew past the page, and the
  Status and Revoke columns were drawn on top of the overflow.

  Hover IS the whole disclosure, so it is a plain `title`: native, zero JS,
  no dialog, and the same way the Media screen hands over a URL too long to
  show. Takes `items` as a list of strings (use the `json_list` filter on a
  stored JSON column).
#}
{%- if items is empty -%}
<span class="mut">—</span>
{%- else -%}
<span class="chips"><span class="chip">{{ items|first }}</span>
{%- if items|length > 1 %}<span class="chip more" title="{{ items|slice(1)|join(', ') }}">+{{ items|length - 1 }}</span>{% endif -%}
</span>
{%- endif -%}